  "aiContextParagraph": "Discussions regarding the selection of a new Vice President to accompany President Prabowo Subianto have intensified following reports of a potential vacancy. Sufmi Dasco Ahmad, currently serving as Deputy Speaker of the House of Representatives, has emerged as a prominent candidate supported by various activists, academics, and political observers. Observers attribute this support to his long history of political loyalty to the President. Additionally, the National Mandate Party has explicitly stated its willingness to back a candidate from the Gerindra Party, leaving the final decision to the President's discretion. Other potential candidates, including leadership figures from the Regional Representative Council, have also been discussed in broader political analysis, but current discourse remains focused on the qualifications and suitability of Dasco for the vice-presidential transition.",
